{
  "description": "`os.config.local-folders` as both shells keep it (ticket 26/09/30 NON-DESTRUCTIVE-HISTORY-EDITING, W2-B follow-up 4 / W2-C follow-up 5): an event-sourced config facet persisted local-only in the shell's own preferences (`semio.os.config` → `preferences[\"os.config.local-folders\"]`, React's `OsShellConfig.setPreference`) as `{version: 1, events}`. `commits` runs mutations from an empty log: a mutation that changes nothing is not recorded; `bindings` is what the log folds to after each step and `log` the stored value after the last. `logs` are stored values and the bindings they replay to — a log that does not read whole (not JSON, another version, an event off the payload schemas) reattaches nothing. `offers` is the reconnect offer for a session's document identity: its binding when the same document in the same program and app is not attached. `names` is the folder name a person knows (the last path segment), `texts` the band's copy (React's `ui.sync.reconnect.*`, normal terminology) for `folder`.",
